From: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: framebuffer: root only off Android

On Android the framebuffer: service's screencap is limited by AID_GRAPHICS
and SELinux. Off Android nothing equivalent applies, so only offer it
when adbd runs as root.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [non-Android adbd policy]

AI-Generated: Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/services.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/services.cpp
@@ -301,6 +301,13 @@ unique_fd daemon_service_to_fd(std::stri
 
 #if defined(__linux__)  // Android, or Linux with build/platform
     if (name.starts_with("framebuffer:")) {
+#if !defined(__ANDROID__)
+        // Off Android nothing like AID_GRAPHICS guards the screen, so only
+        // root gets it.
+        if (getuid() != 0) {
+            return unique_fd{};
+        }
+#endif
         return create_service_thread("fb", framebuffer_service);
     } else if (android::base::ConsumePrefix(&name, "remount:")) {
         std::string cmd = ADBD_REMOUNT_COMMAND " ";
